{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the best result so far at 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1, modestly above RNA-only multiprofile+avgpool (0.591). Image-only is very weak (0.208), so the image modality's contribution in the multimodal setting is uncertain. Question: Does the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) meaningfully affect multimodal performance? config_019 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while holding all other hyperparameters identical to the best config. This is the cleanest single-variable test of whether the image features are being optimally mixed or merely appended. Why best next step: It directly exploits the strongest evidence (config_018) with a minimal, interpretable perturbation, reducing uncertainty about whether the modest multimodal gain is robust to fusion design or an artifact of concat. If weighted fusion improves or matches concat, we gain confidence in the multimodal direction and can then explore other axes (image encoder, RNA encoder); if it degrades, it signals the image channel may be diluting the RNA signal and we should prioritize RNA-encoder improvements instead."
}

